    {
      "id": "claim_c65ff4c09cf74611a54783366b7b7ca6",
      "statement": "Feature 073 (scheduled backups) enforces a distinct, inverse-default SSRF-style guard on user-supplied destination hosts (private/loopback/link-local denied by default, opt-in via BACKUP_ALLOWED_DESTINATION_HOSTS) that is separate from and does not supersede the feature 018 Ollama-URL SSRF guard, which instead allows private/loopback addresses by default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/backup-destination-url-guard.ts#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3bb3042b3b5aa143f8475cc558dfa098e8c2baadc61e05c0b20207f970572b03:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/config/env.ts#L113-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddee6d38cca41554a05d82df091f764e57486c2dc4e819adf46536736d2e36a6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7f080aee71a14be8b234c9db347faf07",
      "statement": "server.js runs outside the Metro/Expo bundle as plain CommonJS and cannot import frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server modules directly, so the backup feature's scheduling clock (a setInterval in server.js) reaches the scheduling logic via a loopback HTTP POST to /bff-api/backups/tick guarded by a shared secret (BACKUP_TICK_SECRET), rather than by calling a function; this tick never fires under `pnpm start` because server.js does not run under Metro.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/README.md#L144-L163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:644a1f55ac0150e9355f8c6645e916219a587b989d61f48b81b2295af1748eb3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L86-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d708d07504f8c9d59e9e977e59dd4474286e6001104253d1e040883a549ae674:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_511f1f481eea40df966a04fac5f7242b",
      "statement": "mongo-client.ts explicitly passes a static `runtimeAdapters: { os }` (imported via `import * as os from 'node:os'`) to the MongoClient constructor to work around a mongodb driver ≥7.6.0 regression where the driver's dynamic `import('os')` promise rejects under Jest's CJS runtime and is silently swallowed, collapsing the client metadata document to `{}` and causing MongoDB to refuse the handshake with a 'Missing required sub-document driver' error that mimics a driver/server incompatibility.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/mongo-client.ts#L26-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:089546ae3836750320f7198c0ccc414853e68aa9e1721c9ca69047806f15bdc4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c323241b900c48039805885c8f8fed48",
      "statement": "The Redis leader lock guarding the scheduled-backup tick (redis-lock.ts) is only an optimisation to avoid duplicate scanning across multiple BFF instances and relies on a TTL guess, so an overrunning run can legitimately lose the lock to another instance while still active; the actual exactly-once guarantee for job execution is a single-document atomic findOneAndUpdate claim in backup-job-store.ts that carries no timing assumption.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/backup-job-store.ts#L76-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4283859fe9896b4971c7798af67c6e84c86af4cf2ec5e7589f8b54ecc39e2d85:"
        },
